[TEXT] All evidence is in. The picture is complete and unambiguous.

**Summary of findings:**
- `br_v5` on `sshswitch` is **administratively DOWN** (`<BROADCAST,MULTICAST>`, no UP/LOWER_UP flags) — this is the VLAN 5 SVI carrying IP 10.5.0.254/24, the default gateway for all VLAN 5 hosts
- Its two member interfaces (`bond0.5` and `eth0.5`) are both fully UP — so the members are fine, only the bridge itself was shut
- `br_v6` (VLAN 6 SVI, 10.6.0.254/24) is fully UP → PC3/PC4 reach their gateway successfully
- PC1 → PC2 ping works (L2 within switch4, never needs the gateway)
- PC1 → 10.5.0.254 returns "Destination Host Unreachable" (gateway unreachable)
- The startup script explicitly runs `ip link set br_v5 up`, so it was brought down post-startup by the injected fault

